There is a lot of traffic on the road.
Then a tourist comes towards me.
He is looking at a map on his phone.
He asks, "Excuse me, where is the metro station?"
I reply, "The metro station is a little far from here."
I point my hand straight ahead.
I say, "You go straight along this road."
"From there, the bus goes straight to the metro station."
"The buses come often."
He asks, "Is it far?"
I say, "By bus, it is not far."
"It takes only about ten minutes."
He smiles.
He says, "Thank you very much."
I smile and say, "You are welcome."
He walks forward.
I walk on my way.
